 2027 capex is up 12%, so it looks fundable through bonds.\n- **Equity is the weak spot.** Two utility share offerings were cut back. Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after demand fell short.\n- **Pellham is the risk.** Pellham's 2027 capex is up 18%, and it is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria. It says it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes \"until financing improves\" (doc `pellham-offering`).\n\n**Gaps in the evidence:**\n- I found no Pellham bond issuance, leverage or rating data. I can't say whether it could replace the withdrawn equity with debt. Its cuts suggest it can't, or won't.\n- The only debt data point is one Norvane deal.\n\n**Net view:** Debt markets can fund the sector's 2027 plans in aggregate, at higher cost. The sector's reliance on debt rather than equity may limit leverage headroom, so some capex slippage is likely. Pellham's cut is the clearest sign of that, and it matters for grid equipment demand.","ttft_ms":1957,"type":"result","duration_ms":19420,"uuid":"c894ccfb-f286-4f78-93a9-78e6943e150b","ttft_stream_ms":970,"time_to_request_ms":72,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":13,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":8,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":8,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":22,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":68,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":205,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":132,"process_rss_mib_result":205,"process_anon_mib_result":124,"process_peak_rss_mib":224,"process_cpu_ms_turn":635,"process_wall_ms_turn":19420,"process_cpu